      "problem": "Evaluate $6\\,\\textrm{i}\\cdot(4 + 2\\,\\textrm{i}).$",
      "worked_solution": "To multiply a complex number by a purely imaginary number, we use the distributive property and the fact that $\\textrm{i}^2 = -1.$\n\nFor the given problem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\,\\text{i}\\cdot (4+2\\,\\text{i}) & =6\\,\\text{i}\\cdot 4+6\\,\\text{i}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{i} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 6\\,\\text{i}+6\\cdot 2\\cdot \\,{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\  & =24\\,\\text{i}+12\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =24\\,\\text{i}-12 \\\\  & =-12+24\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
